An internal admin tool uses server-side sessions. Its logout handler:

@Post("logout")
@HttpCode(204)
logout(@Res({ passthrough: true }) res: Response) {
  res.clearCookie("sid", { path: "/", secure: true, httpOnly: true });
}

Response header: Set-Cookie: sid=; Path=/; Expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT; HttpOnly; Secure

After the click on Logout:

SELECT id, user_id, expires_at FROM admin.sessions WHERE user_id = 'u_7';
--  id      | user_id |       expires_at
-- 9f1c…e2  | u_7     | 2026-10-26 21:00:00+00

Statement: "Because the logout response cleared the sid cookie, a copy of the sid value taken before logout can no longer be used against the admin tool."
